e the way that they operate in a  way where we would need to be really  really quick to keep up with them so  what we felt is that this is a perfect  use case for machine learning where we  could just let a machine do that and if  we had enough data in the background to  to power that  the machines would become more  intelligent and would understand you  know how to spot fraudulent behavior I  actually my colleagues spoke a bit more  about this in in another session I think  it was yesterday and there's a video  which which explains more technically  what we're doing there but you know at a  high level the datasets that we use in  are things like past orders previous  cases of fraud past deliveries the cost  of baskets ordered items so you know  that if someone is effectively every  morning at 9:00 a.m. by in X amounts of  I don't know alcohol and they are just  you know being placed in these random  kind of delivery spots you can assume  that's you know fraudulent activity but  the powerful thing is taking all these  data sets together you get new trends  and you get new ideas and you can  actually for the first time stay ahead  of the fraudulent activity with fraud  what's interesting is in our customer  journey actually we we do our fraud  detection at the front end of that  customer journey so effectively when you  enter the site to start shopping we are  already doing the fraud checks and and  starting to assess fraudulent activity  and that's because you know we want to  make sure that anything that happens  after that is not fraudulent some of the  tools that we use are we really try to  use the whole stack of of google cloud  so we use the ml engine bigquery cloud  storage and tensorflow  and you know this is a really really big  project right now within within our  business this is another diagram which  just gives that whole data flow  so the the last section is customization  so if again you look at the the  end-to-end customer journey where you  start an